---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Building for the Elderly — Pratyush Shrivastav"
  description="Designing mobile experiences for people who were never meant to learn smartphones. A deep dive into UX principles for elderly-first healthcare applications."
>
  <meta property="og:title" content="Building for the Elderly — UX Strategy & Design" slot="head" />
  <meta property="og:description" content="Crafted a UX philosophy and design principles to create an intuitive, safe, and empowering digital experience for elderly users." slot="head" />
  <meta property="og:image" content="https://pm-pratyush.com/elderly-card-image.png" slot="head" />
  <meta property="og:image:width" content="1600" slot="head" />
  <meta property="og:image:height" content="900" slot="head" />
  <meta property="twitter:title" content="Building for the Elderly — UX Strategy & Design" slot="head" />
  <meta property="twitter:description" content="Crafted a UX philosophy and design principles to create an intuitive, safe, and empowering digital experience for elderly users." slot="head" />
  <meta property="twitter:image" content="https://pm-pratyush.com/elderly-card-image.png" slot="head" />
  <meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" slot="head" />
  <section class="work-hero">
    <div class="hero-content-split">
      <div class="hero-text">
        <div class="work-breadcrumb reveal">
          <a href="/">← Back to home</a>
        </div>

        <div class="work-head reveal">
          <span class="kicker kicker--accent">Building for the Elderly</span>
          <h1 class="work-title display">
            Designing mobile experiences for people who were never meant to learn smartphones.
          </h1>
          <p class="work-lede">
            Our mission is to build a digital experience for the elderly that serves them not only functionally but also emotionally with clarity, ease, and respect. Our UX philosophy is rooted in empathy and simplicity. Every interaction should feel intuitive, safe and empowering—even for a first-time smartphone user.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-image reveal">
        <img src="/elderly-ux/elderly-ux-cover.png" alt="Elderly app interface showing health monitoring" />
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="work-content">
    <div class="page">
      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>Our Mission</h2>
        <p>
          Build a digital experience for the elderly that serves them not only functionally but also emotionally with clarity, ease, and respect. Our UX philosophy is rooted in empathy and simplicity. Every interaction should feel intuitive, safe and empowering—even for a first-time smartphone user.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-block reveal">
        <h2>Six Core Principles</h2>
        <p>
          The following principles guide every design decision:
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="principle reveal">
        <div class="principle-text-block">
          <h3>Predictable Navigation</h3>
          <p>We prioritize clarity and consistency in navigation. Every screen should lead somewhere meaningful, with obvious next steps and no dead ends. Users should never feel lost or unsure of how to proceed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-image-block">
          <img src="/elderly-ux/predictable-navigation.png" alt="Clear navigation with large buttons and obvious next steps" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principle reveal">
        <div class="principle-text-block">
          <h3>Design that Respects Hands and Eyes</h3>
          <p>Our design philosophy empathizes with the real-world challenges of the elderly—tremors, reduced dexterity, and visual decline. Touch targets must be large, clear, and comfortably spaced. Text should be comfortably legible, with large fonts that reduce strain and support aging vision. This isn't just about usability—it's about meeting our users where they are and ensuring they feel accommodated, not challenged.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-image-block stacked-images">
          <img src="/elderly-ux/large-components-1.png" alt="Large touch targets and comfortable spacing" />
          <img src="/elderly-ux/large-components-2.png" alt="Comfortable spacing between components" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principle reveal">
        <div class="principle-text-block">
          <h3>Guiding Attention with Visual Hierarchy</h3>
          <p>Every screen must emphasize the most important action or piece of information. Visual hierarchy isn't decoration—it's direction. It should gently guide users toward what matters most.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-image-block stacked-images">
          <img src="/elderly-ux/visual-hierarchy-1.png" alt="Clear visual emphasis on primary action" />
          <img src="/elderly-ux/visual-hierarchy-2.png" alt="Visual hierarchy in action" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principle reveal">
        <div class="principle-text-block">
          <h3>Simplicity with Intent</h3>
          <p>We do not believe in showing less for the sake of minimalism. We believe in showing only what is needed, and when it is needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-image-block">
          <img src="/elderly-ux/simplicity.png" alt="One clear action per screen" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principle reveal">
        <div class="principle-text-block">
          <h3>Conversational Interface</h3>
          <p>Traditional settings menus are replaced with a conversational chatbot flow—not powered by AI, but by thoughtful design. Users will make changes as if speaking to a helper, never facing more than three choices at a time.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-image-block stacked-images three">
          <img src="/elderly-ux/conversational-menu-1.png" alt="Conversational menu flow step 1" />
          <img src="/elderly-ux/conversational-menu-2.png" alt="Conversational menu flow step 2" />
          <img src="/elderly-ux/conversational-menu-3.png" alt="Conversational menu flow step 3" />
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="principle reveal">
        <div class="principle-text-block">
          <h3>Building Confidence, Not Anxiety</h3>
          <p>Elderly users often fear that a wrong tap might cause irreversible harm. Our design must eliminate that anxiety by making every action feel safe and recoverable. Interfaces should reassure users that they are always in control, with clear confirmations, undo options, and fail-safes where needed.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="principle-image-block">
          <img src="/elderly-ux/building-confidence.png" alt="Clear feedback and confirmation messages" />
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .work-hero {
    padding-block-start: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    padding-block-end: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .work-content {
    padding-block-start: clamp(2.5rem, 8vh, 4.5rem);
    padding-block-end: clamp(3rem, 10vh, 5rem);
  }

  .hero-content-split {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-page);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3rem);
    align-items: center;
  }

  @media (min-width: 1000px) {
    .hero-content-split {
      grid-template-columns: 1.1fr 0.95fr;
    }
  }

  .hero-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vh, 2rem);
  }

  .hero-image {
    border-radius: 12px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.1);
  }

  .hero-image img {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
  }

  .work-breadcrumb a {
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-faint);
    text-decoration: none;
    display: inline-block;
    transition: color 250ms;
  }
  .work-breadcrumb a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  .work-title {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vh, 3.2rem);
    max-width: 16ch;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .work-lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 2.4vh, 1.25rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 65ch;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .page {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: var(--w-page);
    margin-inline: auto;
    padding-inline: var(--gutter);
  }

  .content-block {
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 4.5rem);
  }

  .content-block h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .content-block p {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 0 0 1rem 0;
  }

  .content-block p em {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  .principle-list {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  @media (min-width: 760px) {
    .principle-list {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }

  .principle-item {
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--paper-alt);
  }

  .principle-item h3 {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 650;
    margin: 0 0 0.5rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .principle-item p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  .content-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0.8rem;
  }

  .content-list li {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.97rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .content-list li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: 0.65em;
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
  }

  .content-list strong {
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .principle {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vh, 3rem);
    align-items: center;
    padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 6vh, 3.5rem);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    margin-block: 0;
  }

  .principle:first-of-type {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  /* Add margin below sections with stacked images to prevent border overlap */
  .principle:nth-child(3),
  .principle:nth-child(5) {
    margin-bottom: clamp(3rem, 8vh, 5rem);
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .principle {
      grid-template-columns: 1.4fr 1fr;
    }

    .principle:nth-child(even) {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.4fr;
    }

    .principle:nth-child(even) .principle-text-block {
      order: 2;
    }

    .principle:nth-child(even) .principle-image-block {
      order: 1;
    }
  }

  .principle-text-block h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    margin: 0 0 0.8rem 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .principle-text-block p {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    line-height: 1.65;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    margin: 0;
  }

  .principle-image-block {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    position: relative;
  }

  .principle-image-block img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 240px;
    height: auto;
    display: block;
    border-radius: 12px;
    box-shadow: 0 8px 20px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12);
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .principle-image-block img {
      max-width: 220px;
    }
  }

  /* Stacked images layout */
  .principle-image-block.stacked-images {
    position: relative;
    height: 400px;
    margin-top: clamp(2rem, 5vh, 3rem);
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images.three {
    height: 450px;
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images img {
    position: absolute;
    max-width: none;
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images img:nth-child(1) {
    width: 45%;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 40px;
    z-index: 3;
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images img:nth-child(2) {
    width: 50%;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    z-index: 2;
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images.three {
    height: 360px;
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images.three img:nth-child(1) {
    width: 38%;
    left: 0;
    bottom: 80px;
    z-index: 4;
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images.three img:nth-child(2) {
    width: 40%;
    left: 30%;
    bottom: 40px;
    z-index: 3;
  }

  .principle-image-block.stacked-images.three img:nth-child(3) {
    width: 42%;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    z-index: 2;
  }
</style>
